From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Miroshnichenko <serg.zorg@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:45:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: allow high-priority contexts without CAP_SYS_NICE

SteamVR on NixOS runs inside Steam's bubblewrap user namespace, where file
capabilities cannot grant CAP_SYS_NICE to vrcompositor-launcher. The amdgpu
driver then refuses to create a high-priority context and SteamVR disables
asynchronous reprojection. Return 0 from the priority check instead of
-EACCES so the session can always request the high-priority queue, just as
the current DRM master already can.

This removes the CAP_SYS_NICE gate for high-priority GPU contexts: any
process that can open the DRM device may request one. Enable it only on
single-user machines that need VR async reprojection.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ctx.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ctx.c
index d53259a..136d5a5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ctx.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ctx.c
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@ static int amdgpu_ctx_priority_permit(struct drm_file *filp,
 	if (drm_is_current_master(filp))
 		return 0;
 
-	return -EACCES;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static enum amdgpu_gfx_pipe_priority amdgpu_ctx_prio_to_gfx_pipe_prio(int32_t prio)
